# The generated Pages site. NOT tracked, deliberately: build_site.py wipes and rewrites all
# 456 pages on every run, so committing it would put ~4.3 MB of churn in history on every
# corpus change -- on top of research/docs/, which is tracked for a different reason (an
# agent must be able to read a category page straight out of a clone, with no Python).
# Nothing needs this in the repo: GitHub Pages can build it in CI and publish the artifact.
# Rebuild with:  cd research && python3 tools/build_site.py
docs/
